WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.520
In 2018, a truly original horror film called
A Quiet Place premiered at SXSW.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:11.420
The buzz was fast and furious much like the
film's truly terrifying creatures.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.180
Next year, we'll be getting a sequel to A
Quiet Place.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.180
Here's everything we know so far.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.080
“ahhh”

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.640
A few weeks after the U.S. release of A Quiet
Place on April 6th, 2018, Paramount Pictures

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.840
announced that a sequel was officially happening.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.120
This wasn't terribly surprising news after
all, the film was a monster hit right out

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:34.740
of the gate.

00:00:35.129 --> 00:00:39.680
It also happened to be directed by John Krasinski,
a multi-talented actor best known for his

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:40.680
turn in The Office.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.460
"When you were in the office earlier talking
to Wallace, did I come up at all?"

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.040
"Uh…

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.500
Well, we did talk about how handsome you are."

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.640
Krasinski also co-starred and co-wrote the
screenplay for A Quiet Place.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.420
Ultimately, he helmed a thoroughly engaging
fright-fest that was basically begging for

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.460
a follow up, albeit quietly.

00:01:05.229 --> 00:01:09.759
The sequel was originally set to premiere
on May 15th, 2020, but the powers that be

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:12.720
moved up that date to March 20th, 2020.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:16.620
Long story short: We won't have to wait much
longer to see the next installment.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.200
As of the making of this video, the film doesn't
have an official title.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.899
In a July 2019 Twitter post, actor and director
John Krasinski shared a slate from production

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.680
that simply read "Part II," so there's that.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.860
But as of now, the film's title could be pretty
much anything.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:33.800
It could be

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.760
A Quiet Place 2: Keep Quiet

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:38.660
An Even Quieter Place

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.640
A Quiet Place 2: Return to SHH!

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:43.840
The possibilities are endless.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.820
Expect to see some familiar faces in the sequel.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:51.820
In early 2019, it was confirmed that actress
Emily Blunt John Krasinski's wife in real

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.320
life would be returning to play Evelyn Abbott.

00:01:54.509 --> 00:01:59.640
And there's more good news: Co-stars Millicent
Simmonds and Noah Jupe will be back to play

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.340
Regan and Marcus Abbott.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.980
So if you've been eager to catch up with the
Abbott family, you're in luck.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:08.900
However, it's still unclear whether Krasinski
will be appearing in the film.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:11.040
We're... guessing not.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.980
The world of A Quiet Place is… well, it's
very, very quiet.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.500
Except when it's not.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:40.140
“Ahh”

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.970
Throughout the first film, we pretty much
stick with the Abbott family though we do

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.160
meet another ill-fated survivor.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.480
“Ahh”

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:55.760
It's a very brief, very brutal moment… but
it shows us that the Abbotts aren't alone.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.980
As John Krasinski told Deadline in May 2018:

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.080
“The thing that I loved in the movie [...] was
the question of who was on the other end of

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:07.750
those fires, when the father lights the fire
and in the distance those other fires light

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:08.240
up.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:09.480
How did those people survive?”

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.620
Looks like we may find out.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.460
There's going to be some new, totally panicked
faces in the sequel.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.680
In March 2019, Cillian Murphy of Peaky Blinders
was reportedly in talks to join the cast.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.300
"It was meant to be routine."

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:29.200
In June 2019, it was announced that Atlanta
actor Brian Tyree Henry was also cast in the

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.620
film — but scratch that!

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.640
Deadline reported in August 2019 that Djimon
Hounsou was replacing him,

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.600
due to Henry having a scheduling conflict.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:42.960
As we mentioned, John Krasinski didn't just
direct and star in A Quiet Place he also co-wrote

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:43.520
the screenplay.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.020
Although writers Scott Beck and Bryan Woods
are credited with the first film's original

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.360
story, Krasinski ultimately rewrote the script.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.740
This time around, Krasinski is the director
and the sole screenwriter, according to IMDb.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:00.340
That's an exciting development, and we can't
wait to see what he's cooking up for us.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.800
Intriguingly, he told The New York Times in
January 2019:

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:08.800
"I do have sort of a parental feeling about
this movie, and I don’t want A Quiet Place

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.280
to turn into an action movie where 400 people
have machine guns.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.080
Or did I give away the ending to the sequel?"

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.400
Hey, we would totally watch that.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.940
So what exactly do we know about the ghastly
creatures in A Quiet Place?

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.120
Not a whole lot.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:27.760
They're presumably extraterrestrials, and
they obviously have extra-sensitive hearing.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.920
Oh, and they've wiped out most of humanity.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.440
They're kind of a big deal.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.040
Will we be learning more about these vicious
jerks in the sequel?

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:40.800
Before leaving the project, actor Brian Tyree
Henry dropped a rather tantalizing morsel.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.280
In June 2019, he told The Observer:

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:47.560
"I think that we’re also going to get a
few answers to the origin of where and how

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:48.860
this whole thing happened.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.840
I think that people want to know that.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.680
But I think you’re just going to see another
side of it…more of humanity that survived

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:56.820
this thing in this next story."

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.280
And that's all we know about the sequel right
now.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:03.430
John Krasinski and his cohorts have remained
remarkably tight-lipped about the upcoming

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:06.560
horror film which is really rather appropriate,
isn't it?

